branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: VERSION — app now reports 10.40.0 (was hardcoded 10.33.0, never tracked the work). NEW since the live v10.39.0: (1) FILTER-CUTOFF AUTOMATION — Tools ▸ Editors ▸ Automation now has a Filter Cutoff target (a global cutoff multiplier, log-mapped so the lane centre is ×1, octave-symmetric 0.25×…4×) for timbre sweeps; audio-thread-reviewed, off (×1) is bit-identical, auto-resets to neutral when the lane is empty or automation is off. (2) STABLE STEREO IMAGE — synth voices pan by PITCH (key-follow, gentle) instead of by reused voice-slot index, so fast/arpeggiated notes no longer wobble across the field; mono sub anchors the low end. (3) ADAPTIVE BRIGHTNESS — the per-genre brightness lift now scales with how dull the genre already is, so dull genres read brighter (the goal) while bright genres aren't over-brightened/harsh. (4) DEPLOY RESILIENCE — the upload step retries Apple's transient ASC errors (503 / auth / unexpected-content) with backoff. Carries everything from v10.39.0: komische-Töne sound fixes (stranded/off-pitch sub drone + steal portamento) + Automation (master · tempo · cutoff) + MIDI import (melody + GM drums) + Audio Clips + Unison. All Xcode-Compile-Check green per commit; audio-thread + concurrency + DSP reviews on the touched paths.
